**Expert-band design highlights:** cyclic Offer counter-loop (SELLER_COUNTERED↔BUYER_COUNTERED), 3-hop transitive cascade (accept→UNDER_CONTRACT→auto-PENDING), FAILED-contingency compensation invariant, peer-roles RBAC (dual-agency on same listing forbidden), dual-variant net-to-seller (provisional vs final), pinned nested-rounding commission divergence, DTI threshold at exactly 0.43, half-open showing-buffer adjacency boundary, and dual OCC version gates on accept + close.

**Notable Step 7 finding:** the only fix was a launcher/boot-reliability issue — `start.sh` ran `pip install` on every per-test restart, and under 68 restarts × 8 concurrent rounds (~544 contended pip calls) the server couldn't boot inside the runner's restart window, causing a random subset of tests to time out each round. Guarding the install behind an `import flask` check eliminated the flakiness; **no test or behavioral-logic changes were needed**. Step 9 then pinned 9 residual PRD silences/mismatches the test suite never exercised (version init value, several state-gate orderings, net-sheet provisional basis, null-field shapes, div-by-zero handling).

